        <headline>Storm Warning issued September 25 at 1:52AM EDT until September 26 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Gale Warning, north winds 25 to 35 kt with
gusts up to 45 kt and seas 10 to 15 ft. For the Storm Warning,
north winds 30 to 40 kt with gusts up to 50 kt and seas 11 to
16 ft expected.

* WHERE...Coastal waters from Cape May NJ to Cape Henlopen DE
out 20 NM and Coastal waters from Cape Henlopen to Fenwick
Island DE out 20 NM.

* WHEN...For the Gale Warning, until 6 PM EDT this evening. For
the Storm Warning, from 6 PM this evening to 6 PM EDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Storm force winds and hazardous seas will capsize or
damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should remain in port, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for severe conditions.</instruction>
